<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia's Ocampo says coffee premiums hurt sales.</title>
<headline>Colombia's Ocampo says coffee premiums hurt sales.</headline>
<dateline>CARTAGENA, Colombia 1996-11-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finance Minister Jose Antonio Ocampo said Saturday that the high premiums Colombian coffee has fetched in New York over much of the past year were hurting sales and needed to be revised downwards.</p>
<p>The premiums are set by Colombia's National Coffee Growers Committee as part of an export formula aimed at compensating for high production costs and taxes paid by private exporters.</p>
</text>
